                <Pad Id="Ow6OI8m2qB0OVu6D82mDhI" Bounds="696,372,325,306" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="This is a general purpose way to instantiate/update and dispose of whatever the user patched inside a region. Think of this process as a simple lifetime manager of one instance of the users' patch inside the region.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;E.g. this process initializies all users' process nodes inside the region by calling CreateRegionPatch.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;If the user uses process nodes with white pins he might even end up with those being connected to the input border control points. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;We call CreateRegionPatch on Update once in the first frame - instead of on Create - so that we can feed the input border control point values. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;This way the user can actually make use of the border control points within &quot;Create&quot;.">
